203	<h2><span class="num">New in version 6</span>Today's three drafts: a review's findings</h2>
204	<p>At 18:22 you asked where the problem was, after the coordinator put to you, as an ask with options, a decision that the record had settled. The skill does not contradict itself. It has a gap: it says to search the record and to act where the record settles the question, and to put a decision already taken as an item for review, never as a hold, but it says nothing on a review's findings before they reach you. Inside that gap, the coordinator made two errors. Its brief asked the reviewer for every reopened item ready as an ask, with options. And it told you that the position gave no reason, from the entry's text alone, without reading its history.</p>
205	<p>The three drafts below answer the gap and the two errors, one each. They are short and declarative, and they name no case that will go stale. None of them is in the skill.</p>
206	<div class="sources"><span class="label">References</span>
