149	<h2><span class="num">Part 3</span>The drift</h2>
150	<ul>
151	<li>Version 21, on 13 October, changed only the chart.</li>
152	<li>Version 22, on 19 October, changed only the page. It added a line for each of batches 14 to 18, and a list of tokens by batch. It left the language changes at batch 13b, though your ask that day named them.</li>
153	<li>Version 23, on 24 October, made the rest of the changes. It also cut text of version 20 that you kept on 13 October, such as the context study and the priced designs of a batch.</li>
154	<li>Version 24 changed only the chart.</li>
155	</ul>
156	<p>About 5.5K came in that the drift note would take out. About 5K of language changes came in that it keeps.</p>
157	<p>Two points matter most for your choice:</p>
158	<ol>
159	<li>The drift came one landing at a time. To land is to commit a batch&rsquo;s tree to <code>main</code>. Each landing added numbers or status that go stale. The hybrid puts them on a separate page.</li>
160	<li>Her letter links the text on <code>main</code>, so each commit to the text changes what she reads. Under the hybrid, a landing never changes it.</li>
161	</ol>
